p+q+r &=9
\\ pq+pr+qr &=8
\\ pqr &= -2
\end{align*}We want to find $\frac{1}{p^2} + \frac{1}{q^2} + \frac{1}{r^2}=\frac{q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2}{p^2q^2r^2}=\frac{(pq+qr+pr)^2-2pqr(p+q+r)}{(pqr)^2}$ and substituting in the values we know (which is what Vieta did), we get: \[\frac{8^2 - 2(-2)9}{(-2)^2}=25\][/think] <answer>25</answer>

